From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wayne Heaney <wayne.heaney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 03 Jul 2026 00:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] usb: gadget: support vendor-specific descriptors under FunctionFS

The composite gadget core stalls a GET_DESCRIPTOR request for any
descriptor type it does not itself recognise: composite_setup()'s
GET_DESCRIPTOR handler switches on the high byte of wValue and, with no
matching case, leaves value at its -EOPNOTSUPP default and breaks to
check_value: without ever dispatching to the function's ->setup().  The
"punt to the function" (unknown:) fallback is only reached for
unrecognised bRequest values, not for a recognised GET_DESCRIPTOR whose
descriptor sub-type is unknown.

This makes a device-recipient GET_DESCRIPTOR for a vendor descriptor type
(e.g. DisplayLink's 0x5f) structurally unreachable by any FunctionFS
function, because FunctionFS always sits behind composite_setup().  The
DisplayLink host driver on Linux issues exactly such a request
(usb_get_descriptor(udev, 0x5f, ...)) and, when it is stalled, logs
"Unrecognized vendor firmware descriptor" and cannot select its channel.

Route vendor-type descriptor requests to the function's ->setup() instead
of stalling them, and let the FunctionFS descriptor-blob validator accept
vendor-type descriptors rather than rejecting the whole blob with -EINVAL.
Both changes are gated on USB_TYPE_VENDOR, so standard descriptor handling
is unchanged.

Based on doominator42/ZeroKVM's
901-usb-gadget-support-vendor-descriptors.patch, re-based onto the
sun60iw2 6.6 vendor tree.

Signed-off-by: Wayne Heaney <wayne.heaney@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/usb/gadget/composite.c b/drivers/usb/gadget/composite.c
index 4f32698..a279fbb 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/composite.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/composite.c
@@ -1905,6 +1905,15 @@ composite_setup(struct usb_gadget *gadget, const struct usb_ctrlrequest *ctrl)
 				memcpy(req->buf, config->descriptors[0], value);
 			}
 			break;
+		default:
+			/*
+			 * Vendor-specific descriptor types (e.g. DisplayLink's
+			 * 0x5f) are not handled by the composite core; punt to
+			 * the function's ->setup() rather than stalling here.
+			 */
+			if (((w_value >> 8) & USB_TYPE_MASK) == USB_TYPE_VENDOR)
+				goto unknown;
+			break;
 		}
 		break;
 
diff --git a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_fs.c b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_fs.c
index 4a88546..e2c65d7 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_fs.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_fs.c
@@ -2117,6 +2117,10 @@ static int __must_check ffs_do_single_desc(char *data, unsigned len,
 		return -EINVAL;
 
 	default:
+		/* Accept vendor-specific descriptor types in the FFS blob. */
+		if ((_ds->bDescriptorType & USB_TYPE_MASK) == USB_TYPE_VENDOR)
+			return length;
+
 		/* We should never be here */
 		pr_vdebug("unknown descriptor: %d\n", _ds->bDescriptorType);
 		return -EINVAL;
-- 
